ld]:mb-2!"><p>I rebuilt ORESCAN as a mobile-first Next.js app in the same dark and gold style. It has the camera scan, a photo-upload fallback (for when the camera is blocked or there's no HTTPS), the EN/SN toggle, the safety monitor, scan history saved on the device (works offline) and the team card. In the browser, uploading test images, saving a scan to history and testing the alarm all worked.</p>
<p>I changed two parts of your prototype on purpose, because miners might act on what they show:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>The gold numbers now come from the photo, not <code node="[object Object]" class="rounded-md border px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-v0-gray-100 text-label-13-mono font-normal before:hidden after:hidden">Math.random()</code>.</strong> The app counts gold-coloured and quartz-like pixels and checks whether the photo is too dark or blurry. The same photo always gives the same result. Every result says it's only an estimate and must be confirmed with a fire assay. If the photo is too poor to read, it shows "‚Äî" instead of a grade.</li>
<li><strong>The safety monitor no longer shows "SAFE" or made-up gas readings.</strong> It now says no sensor is connected, and gas alarms no longer go off at random during scans. "Test alarm" is clearly labelled as a test and makes its siren sound inside the app, so it works with no internet.</li>
</ul>
<p>Value per ton assumes $100/g with 50% recovery. You can change both in <code node="[object Object]" class="rounded-md border px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-v0-gray-100 text-label-13-mono font-normal before:hidden after:hidden">lib/orescan.ts</code>, along with the colour thresholds. The Shona text is my best attempt, so please have a fluent speaker check it.</p>
<p>You can publish and check your deployments from the top right.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="group/message-list mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl text-label-13 leading-relaxed sm:pb-0 px-2 pb-2"><div class="group/form-container content-center" id="prompt-form"><div class="relative z-10 flex w-full flex-col"><div class="relative z-10"><div class="absolute w-full flex justify-center items-center top-[-40px] pointer-events-none"><div style="opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; transition-property: opacity; transition-duration: 150ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.31, 0.1, 0.08, 0.96); transition-delay: 0ms; will-change: auto;"><button class="v0-btn v0-btn-secondary v0-btn-size-sm rounded-full material-menu h-7 !px-0 text-[13px] font-medium pointer-events-auto" type="button" aria-label="Scroll to bottom" style="transition-property: border-color, background, color; transition-duration: 150ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.31, 0.1, 0.08, 0.96); transition-delay: 0ms; will-change: border-color, background, color;"><div class="relative grid overflow-visible" style="transition-property: width, height; transition-duration: 0s; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.3, 0.1, 0.1, 0.95); transition-delay: 0ms; will-change: width, height; place-items: center; place-content: center; width: auto; height: auto;"><div class="grid-stack" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><span class="flex items-center justify-center min-w-[26px]"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" height="16" width="16" data-slot="geist-icon" style="color: currentcolor;"><path fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" d="m12.06 6.75-.53.53-2.82 2.82a1 1 0 0 1-1.42 0L4.47 7.28l-.53-.53L5 5.69l.53.53L8 8.69l2.47-2.47.53-.53z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></span></div></div></button></div></div></div><div inert="" class="relative flex w-full flex-col origin-bottom" style="transform: translateY(34px); opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; transition-property: 